:::

solutions:
:::{.solution}
$f:\mathbb{R}^2\to\mathbb{R}$ by $f(x,y)=x-y$ is continuous. Thus, $E=f^{-1}(A)$ is Borel. $E^y=\{x\in\mathbb{R}:(x,y)\in E\}=y+A$ which is a null set since $m(y+A)=m(A)=0$. Thus $m\times m(E)=\int m(E^y)dm(y)=0$.
:::

